Track 1: Locusts Graze the Bulkhead
- Story & Context: When the climate coils in Hydroponics Bay 3 ruptured during year sixty-four of the interstellar crossing, thousands of escaped feeder locusts settled onto the warm copper tubes of the ventilation array, producing a rhythmic clicking that mimicked an antique woodblock. Pianist Caridad Vane instantly matched their skittering meter with an improvised minor-ninth montuno, while Maelo MacLeod engaged the chanter drone to drown out the blaring containment sirens. Tape operator Ofelia leaned over the one-take lacquer lathe, etching the track straight to disc as she whispered into the monitor mic, "the iron skin tastes sweet when we lose the sun." The resulting track stands as the accidental birth of the movement, capturing the exact second emergency panic dissolved into communal dance.
