Track 2: "Where Will the Brood Sleep?"
- Story & Context: Recorded in the stifling, 95-degree heat of the lower bilge laundry where illegal silkworm terrariums were kept hidden from ship rationing inspectors, this track captures piper Douglas Matos confessing his grief over never seeing terrestrial soil. Caridad stripped the percussive attack down to soft fingertips caressing slack calfskin congas, allowing the Galician pipe drone to warble with genuine condensation buildup inside its wooden stock. Matos broke protocol during the bridge by singing through his chanter's reed, his cracked, melodic baritone posing the central existential lyric: "we carry wings we will never live to see." The illicit tape became an underground heirloom among the ship's night-shift mechanics, hand-copied from reel to reel on greasy parchment paper.
