Track 3: Azimuth of the Cocoon
- Story & Context: As the generation vessel finally breached the halfway point to Proxima, local folklore swore that discarded insect pupae had ground into dust between the playback capstans, permanently altering the azimuth and pitch of every tape deck in Sector Seven. Tomás Hierro sat at the detuned grand piano in the empty Observatory Dome, tracing a lulling, cyclical timba loop that seemed to hang stationary against the starfield while three piper apprentices sustained a chord of pure low air. Over the muted patter of maracas played with palm seeds, the ship’s elder choir murmured the mythic closing refrain, "spun in darkness, the moth outlives the captain." The track drifted through the shipwide ventilation shafts for forty-eight consecutive cycles, marking the symbolic shedding of Earthly identity.
